      "text": "We are given that $\\tan x = 2$.  If we consider $x$ as the angle of $ACD$ (purple segment on the left of the diagram) when $\\overline{AB}$, $\\overline{BC}$, and $\\overline{AC}$ form a right triangle, then:\n\\[\\tan x = \\frac{\\text{base}}{\\text{height}} = \\frac{AC}{CD} = 2.\\] [asy]\nimport graph;\nsize(180);\ndefaultpen(linewidth(0.8)+fontsize(10));\npair A=9dir(50), B=(-9,0), C=(-4,0), D=(0,-4), E=(3,2);\nD(arc(A,9,90,270));\nD(arc(B,-9,90,-90));\nD(arc(C,-4,270,90));\nD(arc(D,4,270,90));\nD(B--D);\nD(C--D);\n\n标记(Kai)\n\nUsing the tangent addition formula, we get\\begin{align*}\n\\tan\\left(x + \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) &= \\frac{\\tan x+\\tan\\frac{\\pi}{4}}{1-\\tan x\\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}}\\\\\n&= \\frac{2+1}{1-2\\cdot1}\\\\\n&= \\boxed{-3}.\n\\end{align*}. The answer is \\boxed{-3}",
